And before you ask,


00:17:00.502 --> 00:17:02.374
I handcuffed myself
for tactical reasons


00:17:02.548 --> 00:17:04.289
that I do not have time
to explain.


00:17:04.463 --> 00:17:06.334
You shouldn'’t have gone off
on your own.


00:17:06.508 --> 00:17:08.206
We'’re supposed to be a team.


00:17:08.380 --> 00:17:10.599
Sorry, buddy.
I'’m still working on this teamwork thing.


00:17:10.773 --> 00:17:12.297
So now what?


00:17:12.471 --> 00:17:14.647
Well, I'’m not jumping
out of any more helicopters


00:17:14.821 --> 00:17:16.823
until we get some answers
from GUN.


00:17:16.997 --> 00:17:18.564
We need somewhere to regroup.


00:17:20.087 --> 00:17:21.915
I know just the place.


00:17:22.089 --> 00:17:24.483
["Lollipop"
by TEMPURA KIDZ playing]


00:17:30.097 --> 00:17:31.664
[all clapping]


00:17:32.447 --> 00:17:34.188
<i>Hai, chiizu.</i>[yelps]


00:17:34.362 --> 00:17:35.624
It'’s an ambush!


00:17:35.798 --> 00:17:37.800
You'’ll never take us alive,
foul beasts!


00:17:37.974 --> 00:17:40.325
Calm down, Knuckles.
This is a Chao Garden.


00:17:40.499 --> 00:17:43.589
One of the top ten must-see
spots in all of Tokyo!


00:17:43.763 --> 00:17:45.678
It'’s a perfect place
for us to blend in.


00:17:45.852 --> 00:17:47.506
Are you Detective Pikachu?


00:17:47.680 --> 00:17:49.116
Yes, he is!


00:17:49.290 --> 00:17:52.250
[chortles] He does
look like a Pokémon.


00:17:52.424 --> 00:17:53.381
"Pika, pika!" [laughs]


00:17:53.555 --> 00:17:55.340
Commander Walters!


00:17:55.514 --> 00:17:57.298
Sonic.


00:17:57.472 --> 00:18:00.214
Thank God you'’re all okay.
I'’m sure you have questions.


00:18:00.388 --> 00:18:03.087
Just a big ticked-off
red and black one.


00:18:03.261 --> 00:18:04.653
Who was that guy?


00:18:04.827 --> 00:18:07.526
Shadow'’s story
began a lot like yours, Sonic.


00:18:07.700 --> 00:18:10.485
But where you found family
and friends on this planet,


00:18:10.659 --> 00:18:14.185
Shadow found only pain and loss.


00:18:14.924 --> 00:18:17.275
<i>It begins over 50 years ago,</i>


00:18:17.449 --> 00:18:20.582
<i>with a meteor crash </i>
<i>in a quiet corner of Oklahoma.</i>


00:18:20.756 --> 00:18:24.369
<i>The meteorite contained</i>
<i>a life-form.</i>


00:18:27.111 --> 00:18:28.895
<i>The ultimate life-form.</i>


00:18:30.897 --> 00:18:33.378
<i>Shadow'’s power--</i>
<i>his "chaos energy"--</i>


00:18:33.552 --> 00:18:36.555
<i>went far beyond</i>
<i>any living creature.</i>


00:18:39.166 --> 00:18:41.734
<i>The scientist</i>
<i>who discovered him</i> <i>believed this power</i>


00:18:41.908 --> 00:18:44.084
<i>would usher in a new era</i>
<i>for humanity.</i>


00:18:45.607 --> 00:18:48.741
<i>But Shadow'’s power</i>
<i>proved too dangerous.</i>


00:18:51.657 --> 00:18:53.659
<i>A terrible accident</i>
<i>destroyed the lab,</i>


00:18:53.833 --> 00:18:56.096
<i>taking human lives with it.</i>[siren wailing]


00:18:56.270 --> 00:19:00.535
<i>The project leader</i>
<i>was blamed for the incident</i> <i>and imprisoned.</i>


00:19:00.709 --> 00:19:02.363
<i>With the program canceled...</i>[yelps in pain]


00:19:02.537 --> 00:19:05.497
<i>...Shadow was a loose end </i>
<i>no one knew how to deal with.</i>


00:19:06.759 --> 00:19:08.674
<i>Too dangerous</i>
<i>to be walking free,</i>


00:19:08.848 --> 00:19:11.198
<i>too valuable to destroy.</i>


00:19:12.286 --> 00:19:14.462
<i>So I had him placed</i>
<i>into stasis...</i>


00:19:17.161 --> 00:19:19.163
<i>indefinitely.</i>


00:19:21.165 --> 00:19:24.255
Wait a second. If Shadow'’s
been on ice for 50 years,


00:19:24.429 --> 00:19:26.692
someone had to help him escape.True.


00:19:26.866 --> 00:19:28.520
But there'’s only a few people
in the world


00:19:28.694 --> 00:19:30.565
who even know
of Shadow'’s existence.


00:19:37.659 --> 00:19:40.532
[J-pop cover of
"I Want You Back" by Jackson 5 playing]


00:19:40.706 --> 00:19:42.882
[people cheering]


00:19:46.668 --> 00:19:49.105
A live show? Yeah!


00:19:52.848 --> 00:19:54.850
[drones humming]


00:19:58.419 --> 00:19:59.420
Get down!


00:20:05.426 --> 00:20:08.603
[people screaming]


00:20:09.778 --> 00:20:11.650
[groaning]


00:20:14.130 --> 00:20:15.393
Egg drones?


00:20:15.567 --> 00:20:18.265
But Robotnik
is supposed to be dead!


00:20:29.058 --> 00:20:31.322
Konnichi-what?


00:20:33.367 --> 00:20:34.586
[weapons powering up]


00:20:34.760 --> 00:20:36.501
[motorbike revving]


00:20:45.118 --> 00:20:46.772
[tires squeal]


00:20:52.256 --> 00:20:56.347
I'’m sorry, we already had
our big motorcycle chase for the evening.


00:21:01.003 --> 00:21:01.961
Commander Walters!


00:21:02.135 --> 00:21:03.397
[Knuckles grunts]


00:21:03.571 --> 00:21:05.617
[Sonic] Commander Walters,
are you okay?


00:21:06.792 --> 00:21:07.793
Sonic...


00:21:07.967 --> 00:21:09.229
[painful grunt]


00:21:10.404 --> 00:21:11.536
...take this.


00:21:11.710 --> 00:21:13.755
[Sonic] What is it?[Walters] A key...


00:21:14.974 --> 00:21:17.542
to the most powerful weapon
GUN has ever built.


00:21:17.716 --> 00:21:20.240
You'’re the only one I trust
to keep it safe.


00:21:20.414 --> 00:21:22.111
[exhales weakly]


00:21:22.286 --> 00:21:23.591
Commander Walters...


00:21:23.765 --> 00:21:25.289
[sirens, vehicles approaching][gasps]


00:21:29.597 --> 00:21:31.251
[indistinct shouts]


00:21:32.426 --> 00:21:33.906
Alpha team, fan out!


00:21:35.299 --> 00:21:36.691
Do we have eyes?


00:21:37.344 --> 00:21:38.345
Secure the perimeter!


00:21:41.653 --> 00:21:43.002
Medevac is en route.


00:21:43.176 --> 00:21:44.830
[indistinct radio chatter]


00:21:46.832 --> 00:21:48.312
His launch key is missing.


00:21:55.536 --> 00:21:57.756
I knew they couldn'’t be trusted.


00:22:00.019 --> 00:22:01.629
[all exclaiming]


00:22:01.803 --> 00:22:03.239
[Tails] Why are we
running from GUN?


00:22:03.414 --> 00:22:04.893
Aren'’t we on the same team?


00:22:05.067 --> 00:22:06.330
[Sonic] Until we get
more information,


00:22:06.504 --> 00:22:08.201
we'’re not trusting anyone.


00:22:08.375 --> 00:22:10.072
Follow me.Get it... off!


00:22:27.786 --> 00:22:29.788
Hold it right there,
Tokyo Drift!


00:22:29.962 --> 00:22:31.355
Who are you?


00:22:34.227 --> 00:22:36.577
[gasps] It'’s the Goat Milker!


00:22:36.751 --> 00:22:39.014
[mimicking Knuckles]
"It'’s the Goat Milker!"


00:22:39.188 --> 00:22:41.234
Relax.
I'’m not here to fight.


00:22:41.408 --> 00:22:44.455
Then why are you here?And why did you free Shadow?


00:22:44.629 --> 00:22:46.544
Are you kidding?


00:22:46.718 --> 00:22:50.330
The last thing we want
is more super-powered hedgehogs running around.


00:22:50.504 --> 00:22:52.463
The doctor had nothing
to do with it.


00:22:54.160 --> 00:22:55.988
And I can prove it.[car alarm chirps]


00:23:11.395 --> 00:23:13.005
Please,


00:23:13.179 --> 00:23:14.223
join me in the crab.


00:23:15.790 --> 00:23:18.967
[narrator] <i>And now back to... </i>
<i>"La UÚltima Pasión."</i>


00:23:19.141 --> 00:23:20.839
I have fallen in love
with another.


00:23:21.013 --> 00:23:22.797
[gasps]


00:23:22.971 --> 00:23:26.235
But who, Gabriella?
Tell me who!


00:23:28.063 --> 00:23:30.196
My twin brother, Pablo?


00:23:31.415 --> 00:23:32.851
<i>Pablo!</i>


00:23:34.766 --> 00:23:36.158
!¡Bastardo!


00:23:36.332 --> 00:23:38.726
Buenos días, !¡hermano!


00:23:38.900 --> 00:23:40.032
<i>No!</i>


00:23:40.206 --> 00:23:42.338
[cackling]


00:23:42.513 --> 00:23:44.819
Let that be a lesson
to you, Juan.


00:23:44.993 --> 00:23:46.560
[beeping]Family


00:23:46.734 --> 00:23:49.955
is a field
of emotional claymores


00:23:50.129 --> 00:23:52.348
that leave you abandoned,
betrayed


00:23:54.133 --> 00:23:57.005
and weeping
while you eat cake,


00:23:57.179 --> 00:23:59.573
which creates copious amounts
of adipose tissue,


00:23:59.747 --> 00:24:02.750
and what some calloused
individuals refer to as...


00:24:02.924 --> 00:24:05.536
[sniffs deeply]
...man boobs.


00:24:05.710 --> 00:24:06.885
Ha.


00:24:08.800 --> 00:24:11.063
[up-tempo Latin jazz playing]


00:24:16.242 --> 00:24:17.852
[slapping along
with the congas]


00:24:20.420 --> 00:24:21.987
[trilling loudly]


00:24:23.118 --> 00:24:24.511
[shrieking]


00:24:24.685 --> 00:24:26.731
Doctor,
we have visitors.


00:24:28.210 --> 00:24:30.212
Really?


00:24:30.386 --> 00:24:33.085
I thought I was having
an anthropomorphic nightmare.


00:24:33.259 --> 00:24:34.739
Where the only person
I could trust in the world


00:24:34.913 --> 00:24:36.436
showed up with
all my worst enemies,


00:24:36.610 --> 00:24:38.307
while I was in a bathrobe,


00:24:38.482 --> 00:24:40.745
playing congas
on my big, fat belly!


00:24:40.919 --> 00:24:42.181
Sorry, sir.


00:24:42.355 --> 00:24:44.488
I don'’t believe it.
Eggman'’s alive?


00:24:44.662 --> 00:24:47.012
And he'’s never
looked worse.


00:24:47.186 --> 00:24:49.493
[cackling] Well, maybe,


00:24:49.667 --> 00:24:53.540
this is what not giving a damn
what you think I look like looks like.


00:24:53.714 --> 00:24:56.935
Sir, right now we have
an even bigger problem.


00:24:57.109 --> 00:24:58.502
Oh, come on.


00:25:00.634 --> 00:25:02.941
There'’s an imposter out there
using your technology.


00:25:03.115 --> 00:25:06.422
Imposter.
That'’s impossi-- What?


00:25:06.597 --> 00:25:08.076
No.


00:25:08.250 --> 00:25:12.298
My sweet mechanized spawn!


00:25:12.472 --> 00:25:16.084
Whomever this party-pooping
posse is looking for


00:25:16.258 --> 00:25:18.565
has stolen my persona


00:25:18.739 --> 00:25:22.090
and the precious babies
from my egg sac.


00:25:22.787 --> 00:25:24.266
Well...


00:25:24.440 --> 00:25:28.836
I'’ll soon egg-xact
my revenge.


00:25:29.010 --> 00:25:30.664
You see what I did there?[chuckles]


00:25:30.838 --> 00:25:34.059
It'’s time for the dramatic
soap-opera twist,


00:25:34.233 --> 00:25:38.367
where this Pablo
reveals his Juan!


00:25:38.542 --> 00:25:42.415
By cross-referencing
the precise coordinates


00:25:42.589 --> 00:25:45.331
of each drone'’s
energy spikes,


00:25:46.071 --> 00:25:48.203
I can track my babies


00:25:48.377 --> 00:25:50.989
to the imposter'’s
base of operations,


00:25:51.163 --> 00:25:52.556
right about...


00:25:52.730 --> 00:25:53.557
there!


00:25:53.731 --> 00:25:55.471
Sonic, I hate to say it,


00:25:55.646 --> 00:25:57.822
but I think we'’re both
after the same person.


00:25:57.996 --> 00:26:00.433
Hold on, hold on.
You'’re not suggesting we team up


00:26:00.607 --> 00:26:02.914
with Doctor Ro-Butt-Stink,
are you?


00:26:03.088 --> 00:26:04.524
Perhaps the fox is right.


00:26:04.698 --> 00:26:07.571
It could be our only chance
to find this mysterious,


00:26:07.745 --> 00:26:09.137
more impressive hedgehog.


00:26:09.311 --> 00:26:10.486
[groans]


00:26:10.661 --> 00:26:12.706
All right, Egghead.
I hate to say it,


00:26:12.880 --> 00:26:14.447
but it looks like
we'’re partners.


00:26:15.579 --> 00:26:17.493
On one condition.


00:26:18.973 --> 00:26:21.541
Dude, you have serious issues.


00:26:21.715 --> 00:26:22.803
Ow!


00:26:25.023 --> 00:26:26.459
[gibbering spasm]


00:26:26.633 --> 00:26:27.808
Let'’s...


00:26:28.592 --> 00:26:29.723
do this!


00:26:29.897 --> 00:26:31.595
["Firestarter"
by The Prodigy playing]


00:26:38.340 --> 00:26:39.472
[pained groan]


00:26:53.007 --> 00:26:54.922
[door thuds][Robotnik grunting]


00:26:56.097 --> 00:26:57.316
Suck it in!


00:26:57.490 --> 00:26:58.665
[grunting][door rattling]


00:26:59.840 --> 00:27:01.189
Tinker-tailor?


00:27:01.363 --> 00:27:02.800
I need room.


00:27:02.974 --> 00:27:05.629
Think Elvis, circa 1976.


00:27:05.803 --> 00:27:08.066
But sir, I don'’t have
the proper materials.


00:27:09.110 --> 00:27:10.459
Found some.


00:27:12.984 --> 00:27:14.159
Resourceful.


00:27:16.596 --> 00:27:18.511
[thunder rumbling]


00:27:42.013 --> 00:27:44.015
[faint, indistinct chatter]


00:27:54.678 --> 00:27:56.767
Hey! This is a restricted area.


00:27:56.941 --> 00:27:59.204
Oh, it'’s okay.
She'’s the professor'’s granddaughter.


00:27:59.378 --> 00:28:01.510
He takes her everywhere.


00:28:01.685 --> 00:28:04.775
Welcome to the lab, Maria.
I'’m Captain Walters.


00:28:04.949 --> 00:28:06.341
Oh, do you know
where my room is?


00:28:06.515 --> 00:28:08.082
Yeah, down the hall
and to the right.


00:28:08.256 --> 00:28:09.780
Make yourself at home.


00:28:09.954 --> 00:28:11.129
But, um,


00:28:11.303 --> 00:28:13.087
let'’s lose the skates,
okay, kiddo?


00:28:13.261 --> 00:28:14.698
Okay.


00:28:19.615 --> 00:28:22.096
[machinery humming softly]


00:28:35.588 --> 00:28:37.721
[fluid bubbling faintly]


00:28:51.082 --> 00:28:52.561
[light chuckle]


00:29:00.526 --> 00:29:01.570
[chuckles]


00:29:02.920 --> 00:29:04.660
[bag rustling]


00:29:06.662 --> 00:29:07.925
[pen uncaps]


00:29:24.376 --> 00:29:25.681
[laughs]


00:29:46.224 --> 00:29:49.096
["End of the Line"
by the Traveling Wilburys playing]


00:30:14.295 --> 00:30:15.470
[delighted shriek]


00:30:15.644 --> 00:30:17.472
[squealing]


00:30:25.176 --> 00:30:26.003
[gasps]


00:30:26.177 --> 00:30:27.134
[yelling]


00:30:31.922 --> 00:30:33.097
[whooping]


00:30:34.925 --> 00:30:36.100
Look out!


00:30:37.666 --> 00:30:38.842
[crashing]


00:30:55.336 --> 00:30:56.772
[faint roaring]


00:31:14.486 --> 00:31:16.662
[song ends]


00:31:16.836 --> 00:31:18.925
[crickets chirping softly]


00:31:20.013 --> 00:31:21.188
Wow.


00:31:21.885 --> 00:31:23.321
Look at all those stars.


00:31:25.149 --> 00:31:26.977
They'’re like diamonds.


00:31:28.674 --> 00:31:30.415
My grandfather says


00:31:30.589 --> 00:31:32.243
it can take hundreds of years


00:31:32.417 --> 00:31:34.419
for the light of a star
to reach Earth.


00:31:35.159 --> 00:31:37.030
And by the time you see it,


00:31:37.204 --> 00:31:39.511
the star might not even
exist anymore.


00:31:41.034 --> 00:31:42.514
Isn'’t that crazy?


00:31:43.994 --> 00:31:45.865
A light shines,


00:31:46.039 --> 00:31:47.998
even though the star is gone.


00:31:49.564 --> 00:31:51.392
Yeah, it does.


00:31:53.220 --> 00:31:54.918
I wonder which one
you came from, Shadow.


00:31:55.092 --> 00:31:55.962
I don'’t know.


00:31:57.094 --> 00:31:59.574
I don'’t know anything
about my home.


00:31:59.748 --> 00:32:02.142
This is your home, Shadow.


00:32:02.882 --> 00:32:04.014
Earth.


00:32:10.934 --> 00:32:12.239
Maria,


00:32:12.892 --> 00:32:14.589
do you think I'’m...


00:32:15.547 --> 00:32:16.809
dangerous?


00:32:18.071 --> 00:32:19.899
What are you talking about?


00:32:20.073 --> 00:32:22.641
The way the scientists
look at me,


00:32:22.815 --> 00:32:24.512
I can tell they'’re afraid.


00:32:24.686 --> 00:32:28.255
Like I'’m the horrible thing
from that movie we watched.


00:32:29.343 --> 00:32:30.779
I don'’t know...


00:32:31.476 --> 00:32:32.956
what I am.


00:32:38.222 --> 00:32:39.788
You'’re my friend.


00:32:41.138 --> 00:32:43.792
And you can do or be
anything you want.


00:32:44.968 --> 00:32:46.578
Not because of your powers,


00:32:46.752 --> 00:32:50.190
but because of who you are...
in here.


00:32:53.019 --> 00:32:55.195
I don'’t know what I'’d do
without you.


00:33:04.988 --> 00:33:07.991
["End of the Line" resumes]


00:33:12.473 --> 00:33:14.171
[song ends abruptly]


00:33:14.345 --> 00:33:15.999
[dust crackling]


00:33:32.841 --> 00:33:34.452
[footfalls]


00:33:37.107 --> 00:33:38.804
Professor?


00:33:38.978 --> 00:33:42.025
It'’s good to see you,
Shadow.


00:33:42.199 --> 00:33:44.288
I knew you'’d come home.


00:33:44.462 --> 00:33:47.030
I can'’t get her out of my head.


00:33:47.204 --> 00:33:48.727
The pain...


00:33:48.901 --> 00:33:50.250
It'’s too much.


00:33:50.424 --> 00:33:53.906
And that is why
we have to punish them.


00:33:58.432 --> 00:34:00.043
Okay, I don'’t like you
and you don'’t like me.


00:34:00.217 --> 00:34:02.045
Let'’s get this
over with quickly.


00:34:02.219 --> 00:34:04.047
Out of my way, dorkupine.


00:34:04.221 --> 00:34:06.310
"Dorkupine"?
Really clever.


00:34:10.749 --> 00:34:12.620
[hollow tapping]


00:34:12.794 --> 00:34:14.883
This door is six-inch-thick
solid steel


00:34:15.058 --> 00:34:16.842
on a pressurized latch.


00:34:17.016 --> 00:34:19.192
I'’ll need a moment to calculate
the molecular density


00:34:19.366 --> 00:34:20.976
and invert
the venting mechanics.


00:34:21.151 --> 00:34:22.587
[thunderous crash]


00:34:24.632 --> 00:34:25.894
[Knuckles] I unlocked it.


00:34:26.069 --> 00:34:29.072
[Robotnik] Subtle as always,
fist-for-brains.


00:34:30.334 --> 00:34:32.075
Easy, Shadow.


00:34:32.249 --> 00:34:34.729
Those are the guests
I'’ve been expecting.


00:34:34.903 --> 00:34:37.558
Let'’s give them
a warm welcome.


00:34:41.388 --> 00:34:42.737
[Stone] Whoa.


00:34:42.911 --> 00:34:44.174
What is this place?


00:34:44.348 --> 00:34:46.306
[Sonic] It looks like
a military base,


00:34:46.480 --> 00:34:48.308
but nobody'’s been here
for years.


00:34:48.482 --> 00:34:49.875
I wonder if it'’s haunted.


00:34:50.049 --> 00:34:52.965
Haunted? Nobody said anything
about being haunted.


00:34:53.139 --> 00:34:56.099
What'’s the matter?
You afraid of g-g-g-ghosts?


00:34:56.273 --> 00:34:58.362
Nothing scares
an Echidna warrior.


00:34:58.536 --> 00:35:00.929
Uh, yeah. Do you remember
what happened last movie night?


00:35:01.104 --> 00:35:02.670
[screaming in terror]


00:35:02.844 --> 00:35:04.150
[piercing scream][all yelling]


00:35:04.324 --> 00:35:05.760
Let go, let go, let go!


00:35:05.934 --> 00:35:08.633
There is no such thing
as a friendly ghost.


00:35:10.200 --> 00:35:11.723
[Sonic]
So which way do we go?


00:35:11.897 --> 00:35:15.596
I know! We should split up.


00:35:15.770 --> 00:35:18.991
Everyone with hideous,
brightly-colored fur take the left and the middle.


00:35:19.165 --> 00:35:20.775
Stone and I will go right.


00:35:20.949 --> 00:35:22.690
No, no, no, no, no. I'’m not
letting you out of my sight.


00:35:22.864 --> 00:35:24.649
Tails, you and Stone go left.


00:35:24.823 --> 00:35:27.913
Knuckles, you take the middle.
Eggman, you and me go right.


00:35:28.087 --> 00:35:30.002
By all means.


00:35:30.176 --> 00:35:31.656
We could use some
time together.


00:35:31.830 --> 00:35:33.440
To work on
your trust issues.


00:35:33.614 --> 00:35:36.443
You know what? You'’re right.
I should be more trusting.


00:35:36.617 --> 00:35:39.403
I mean, you'’ve only tried
to kill me twice!


00:35:41.448 --> 00:35:43.668
Just a dark, creepy hallway.


00:35:43.842 --> 00:35:45.539
Nothing to be afraid of.


00:35:47.280 --> 00:35:48.977
You hear that, ghost?


00:35:49.152 --> 00:35:50.675
You don'’t frighten me!


00:35:50.849 --> 00:35:52.416
[steam hissing][yells]


00:35:55.158 --> 00:35:57.551
Get... a... grip.


00:35:58.465 --> 00:36:00.206
Boo.[screams]


00:36:02.904 --> 00:36:05.603
I'’m just gonna
come right out and say this:


00:36:05.777 --> 00:36:08.562
You'’re adorable.[chuckles]
Oh, um, thanks.


00:36:08.736 --> 00:36:12.175
So, what'’s it like
being Sonic'’s assistant?


00:36:12.349 --> 00:36:15.656
You have a daily routine?
Paid time off? Benefits?


00:36:15.830 --> 00:36:19.007
Oh, I'’m not Sonic'’s assistant.
We'’re teammates.


00:36:19.182 --> 00:36:21.184
He'’s the leader,
Knuckles is the muscle,


00:36:21.358 --> 00:36:22.924
and I'’m the gadget guy.


00:36:23.098 --> 00:36:24.448
We all have a role to play.


00:36:24.622 --> 00:36:26.363
That'’s what makes the team
so special!


00:36:26.537 --> 00:36:28.278
That and the fact
we'’re best friends.


00:36:29.017 --> 00:36:30.323
You are?


00:36:30.497 --> 00:36:32.325
Well, yeah.
Just like you and Eggman, right?


00:36:34.153 --> 00:36:36.199
Uh... Yeah, eh...


00:36:36.373 --> 00:36:38.375
Of course! Yes.


00:36:38.549 --> 00:36:41.421
Me and the doctor,
best of friends.


00:36:42.901 --> 00:36:44.468
That'’s definitely
what we are.


00:36:44.642 --> 00:36:46.774
[metallic clattering]


00:36:46.948 --> 00:36:48.733
[squeaking]


00:36:49.690 --> 00:36:50.735
Hmm.


00:36:55.740 --> 00:36:57.481
[both screaming]


00:37:09.841 --> 00:37:13.410
Whoa. Look at all this stuff.


00:37:13.584 --> 00:37:16.717
This was more than
just a military base or a lab.


00:37:17.283 --> 00:37:18.719
It was a home.


00:37:18.893 --> 00:37:20.460
People lived here.


00:37:21.069 --> 00:37:22.549
He had a family.


00:37:23.289 --> 00:37:25.117
Is that what I smell?


00:37:25.291 --> 00:37:28.381
The stench
of domestic harmony?


00:37:28.555 --> 00:37:32.080
You ever wonder what
your life would have been like if you had a family?


00:37:32.255 --> 00:37:33.691
Hmm... No!


00:37:33.865 --> 00:37:35.867
Maybe you wouldn'’t have gone
full supervillain.


00:37:36.041 --> 00:37:38.870
I have no parents,
no aunts, no uncles.


00:37:39.044 --> 00:37:41.568
And something about my attitude
renders me...


00:37:42.526 --> 00:37:46.660
undesirable
to all possible genders.


00:37:48.532 --> 00:37:50.708
My future is a cul-de-sac!


00:37:51.709 --> 00:37:53.711
The Robotnik name ends...


00:37:55.365 --> 00:37:57.018
<i>avec moi.</i>


00:37:57.192 --> 00:37:59.238
Yes, I know French.


00:38:00.283 --> 00:38:01.762
[shuddering spasm]


00:38:03.764 --> 00:38:04.852
Whoa.


00:38:05.026 --> 00:38:08.029
Is this where you grew up,
Shadow?


00:38:08.203 --> 00:38:09.988
No wonder you'’re so mad.


00:38:10.162 --> 00:38:13.034
